Then test the first genuinely harder variant:
\[
h^M,0^{N_0},\ell_0,0^{N_1},\ell_1,\ldots,0^{N_r},\ell_r,0^L,h
\]
with varying \(\ell_j\). That is where early front-loading constraints may become real.
